                        "sense_id": "a9bd7f01-cc7a-372c-ad2a-da576f4d1276",
                        "entry_id": "28386eda-4462-3517-ab46-35edeed4fb4c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A pig, especially a piglet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cee6dd7c-ce6a-4e18-9229-f9659d5514d0",
                                "sense_id": "a9bd7f01-cc7a-372c-ad2a-da576f4d1276",
                                "text": "The women do most of the business, the men condescending to attend to such matters as the sale of goats, or an occasional “snorker,” which is led by a string, and invariably lends its voice to the general uproar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec84dfa0-2ce4-474f-ad33-ee32818c06cd",
                                "sense_id": "a9bd7f01-cc7a-372c-ad2a-da576f4d1276",
                                "text": "He told me he had got a queer critter that had come to his garden, and to his mind it was very like a little pig—in fact, “fust off he reckoned it was one o’ his young snorkers hed got out. He’s gone to his home now,” he added; […] He seemed to have no fear—he had evidently never been disturbed since he first made his home close to; and had he not been attracted by the grunts of the cottager’s young snorkers, his proximity would never have been suspected."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09fc8311-dba5-4f83-ac66-dade49d1df53",
                                "sense_id": "a9bd7f01-cc7a-372c-ad2a-da576f4d1276",
                                "text": "OH, ’twas Christmas Eve, and, by your leave, / I’ll tell you a wond’rous tale; / For the moreporks porked and the snorkers snorted, / And the tom-cats wailed a wail."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38e1b590-951e-4216-ace6-468daec380b4",
                                "sense_id": "a9bd7f01-cc7a-372c-ad2a-da576f4d1276",
                                "text": "With the aid of a heavy chair he had the pig bailed up in a corner and hog-tied in no time at all. Put into a sack, the young snorker was carried back to captivity."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67ec3103-9179-3c07-9547-6f10a94e588a",
                        "entry_id": "28386eda-4462-3517-ab46-35edeed4fb4c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sausage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d2605af-ee78-4487-930a-9d0f5967342e",
                                "sense_id": "67ec3103-9179-3c07-9547-6f10a94e588a",
                                "text": "[…] a snorker left on the plate. Sam groans, but obediently sinks his fork into a third sausage […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6378fb27-ebf8-4b32-962a-b5e9e2508eeb",
                                "sense_id": "67ec3103-9179-3c07-9547-6f10a94e588a",
                                "text": "Tim is told off for trying to smuggle Dad a 'snorker' (sausage) from the catering trolley."
                            }
                        ]
